 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_cbb3ifx",
   "entryDay": 41,
   "cause": "the expedition",
   "lines": [
    "d41: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Alejandro Bah is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d41: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d41: 🕯️ Alejandro Bah is dead — the expedition. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d41: What Alejandro kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d41: \"Alejandro's gone.\" Esther looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Alejandro.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d41: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Vikram blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Anatomy (Level 1). You know where the important bits are. Arteries, joints, organs. Useful for healing or hurting.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Calming Panic (Level 1). Ground them: 5 things you see, 4 you hear, 3 you touch. Breathe with them. Slow is fast.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Managing Fear (Level 1). Fear is data, not orders. Acknowledge it, then decide anyway. Courage is fear that kept going.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Steady Hands (Level 1). Fine work under pressure. Dressing game, stitching wounds, tying snares — no shake.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Animal Behavior (Level 1). Most animals flee. Give them an escape route and they take it. Cornered animals fight.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Field Dressing (Level 1). Break down game fast and clean. Less waste, more meat, usable parts.",
    "d41: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d41: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Alejandro Bah, 41 days. The mantle passes to Vikram Szymanski.",
    "d41: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Vikram Szymanski, 20 — a paramedic. Their hands know different work now: The Touch, Dowsing, War Cry, Green Whisper, Echo Location.",
    "d41: The village's quarrel was with Alejandro — and Alejandro is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d41: At the grave, Esther, Stan, Ingrid and 4 more speak for Vikram — \"Alejandro trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d41: The fire knew Vikram before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_8kl4txi",
   "entryDay": 42,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d42: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Vikram Szymanski is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d42: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d42: 🕯️ Vikram Szymanski is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d42: What Vikram kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d42: \"Vikram's gone.\" Stan looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Vikram.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d42: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Esther blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d42: 📖 LEARNED: Reading Tracks (Level 1). Fresh tracks have sharp edges. Old tracks crumble. You can tell how recently something passed.",
    "d42: 📖 LEARNED: Reading People (Level 1). Microexpressions leak truth. Watch the eyes, not the mouth. People tell you who they are.",
    "d42: ⚡ TECHNIQUE UNLOCKED: Deep Read! You don't just read trust — you read intent. Know what they'll do next. (Your knowledge of Reading People amplifies your open_book.)",
    "d42: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d42: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Vikram Szymanski, 42 days. The mantle passes to Esther Ramos.",
    "d42: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Esther Ramos, 47 — an aquarium keeper. Her hands know different work now: Beast-calm, Echo Location, Green Whisper.",
    "d42: You knew Vikram — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting them, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d42: At the grave, Stan, Ingrid, Lucas and 3 more speak for Esther — \"Vikram trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d42: The fire knew Esther before the Codex did — her name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_8spi30n",
   "entryDay": 58,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d58: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Esther Ramos is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d58: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d58: 🕯️ Esther is dead — and the dead hold no treaties. Every link Haven has shakes.",
    "d58: Stonebridge watches to see if Haven holds without its dead. The bond is young — they're still deciding what Haven is, and grief delays the verdict. They'll test the link — count on it, unless Haven answers first: send grain (1,500 kcal), send a speaker (2 days), or let the silence answer.",
    "d58: 🕯️ Esther Ramos is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d58: What Esther kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d58: \"Esther's gone.\" Ethan looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Esther.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d58: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Hassan blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d58: 📖 LEARNED: Food Preservation (Level 1). Salt, smoke, dry. The big three. Salt draws water out; bacteria can't live without it.",
    "d58: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d58: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Esther Ramos, 58 days. The mantle passes to Hassan Ali.",
    "d58: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Hassan Ali, 42 — a Butcher. His hands know different work now: Green Whisper, Beard Moss.",
    "d58: The village's quarrel was with Esther — and Esther is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d58: You knew Esther — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting her, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d58: At the grave, Fritz, Stan, Ingrid and 3 more speak for Hassan — \"Esther trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d58: The fire knew Hassan before the Codex did — his name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "hassan_ali",
   "entryDay": 65,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d65: 📓 Codex: you've heard of Pocket Sand. Someone, somewhere, can do this. Now you know its name.",
    "d65: ◈ THE SYSTEM has been watching Fritz — Strange 1. Three offers; they took Pocket Sand. Earned, chosen. (pocket_sand: villager level-up)",
    "d65: 📓 Codex: Fritz chose Pocket Sand (pocket_sand) at Strange 1.",
    "d65: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Hassan Ali is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d65: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d65: 🕯️ Hassan is dead — and the dead hold no treaties. Every link Haven has shakes.",
    "d65: 🕯️ Hassan Ali is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
